{"questions":[{"question_id":"y1UryBRsCjhG35ZV","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"concentration-terms","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"292-ww-hcl-stock-solution-has-density-of-125-g-ml-1-2012-marks-3-y1urybrscjhg35zv.htm","content":"29.2 % (w/w) HCl stock solution has density of 1.25 g mL<sup>-1</sup> . The molecular weight of HCl is 36.5 g mol<sup>-1</sup> .\nThe volume (mL) of stock solution required to prepare a 200 mL solution of 0.4 M HCl is","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<p>To calculate the volume of the 29.2% (w/w) HCl stock solution needed to prepare a 200 mL solution of 0.4 M HCl, we need to use several steps involving concentration and density conversions.</p>\n\n<p>First, we calculate the mass of HCl that is contained in the 200 mL of a 0.4 M solution:</p>\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"50.315ex\" height=\"2.161ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 22239.4 955\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D440\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D440\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1051,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1580,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D460\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D460\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2049,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D460\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D460\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2795.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3851